33 750 202 750C196 750 191 749 185 748C112 736 56 654 56 548C56 465 88 402 136 369C155 357 175 347 202 347C243 347 274 374 293 403C319 441 332 486 332 548C332 608 319 641 319 641M245 693C275 663 292 613 292 548C292 483 275 434 245 404C231 390 221 385 207 385L203 385C182 385 177 391 165 403C136 432 132 478 132 548C132 618 135 662 163 693C174 705 185 712 200 712C223 712 232 706 245 693M500 146C500 63 532-1 580-34C599-46 619-56 646-56C687-56 718-29 737 0C763 38 776 84 776 146C776 208 763 253 737 292C718 319 687 347 647 347C641 347 635 346 629 345C556 333 500 252 500 146M689 290C719 260 736 211 736 146C736 81 719 31 689 1C675-13 665-18 651-18L647-18C638-18 636-18 630-16C607-6 589 20 582 55C577 79 577 90 577 146C577 222 578 257 607 290C618 302 629 309 644 309C667 309 676 303 689 290Z\"></path></defs></svg>","mathFallback":false,"description":"JEE Main's 2023 JEE Main 2023 (Online) 10th April Morning Shift Paper's All Questions with solutions provider ExamSIDE.Com","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 10th April Morning Shift","nextq":"1lgyhrwmm","prevq":"1lgyhf41e","questions":[{"question_id":"1lgyhl1dn","chapter":"chemical-equilibrium","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2023-online-10th-april-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 10th April Morning Shift","permalink":"pthe-number-of-correct-statements-involving-equilibria-in-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-e4lwxfalnklherqz","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>The number of correct statement/s involving equilibria in physical processes from the following is ________</p>\n<p>(A) Equilibrium is possible only in a closed system at a given temperature.</p>\n<p>(B) Both the opposing processes occur at the same rate.</p>\n<p>(C) When equilibrium is attained at a given temperature, the value of all its parameters became equal.</p>\n<p>(D) For dissolution of solids in liquids, the solubility is constant at a given temperature.</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"3","explanation":"<p><b>(A) Equilibrium is possible only in a closed system at a given temperature.</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This statement is true. In a closed system, there is no exchange of matter with the surroundings. This allows the reaction to reach equilibrium at a constant temperature.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>(B) Both the opposing processes occur at the same rate.</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This statement is true. At equilibrium, the forward and reverse reactions occur at the same rate, meaning the concentrations of reactants and products remain constant.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>(C) When equilibrium is attained at a given temperature, the value of all its parameters became equal.</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This statement is false. When a system reaches equilibrium, it doesn&#39;t mean that the values of all parameters (such as the concentrations of reactants and products) are equal. It means that these values are constant, i.e., they are not changing with time because the rates of the forward and reverse reactions are equal.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>(D) For dissolution of solids in liquids, the solubility is constant at a given temperature.</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This statement is true. The solubility of a solid in a liquid (in a saturated solution) is indeed constant at a given temperature and pressure.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, there are 3 correct statements: (A), (B), and (D).</p>\n"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>भौतिक प्रक्रमों के साम्य के संदर्भ में निम्न में से सत्य कथन/नों की संख्या है:</p>\n<p>(A) किसी दिए गए तापमान पर, साम्यावस्था केवल बंद निकाय में ही संभव है।</p>\n<p>(B) दोनों विपरीत प्रक्रम समान दर पर होते हैं।</p>\n<p>(C) किसी दिए गए तापमान पर जब साम्यावस्था प्राप्त होती है तो इसके सभी मापदंडों का मान बराबर होता है।</p>\n<p>(D) द्रवों मे ठोसो के घुलने के संदर्भ में, किसी दिए गए तापमान पर विलेयता स्थिर होती है।</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"3","explanation":null}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"le-chateliers-principle-and-factors-affecting-chemical-equilibrium","type":"integer","year":2023,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["multi_statements"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2023-online-10th-april-morning-shift","active":true},{"question_id":"1lgyhlpij","chapter":"chemical-bonding-and-molecular-structure","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2023-online-10th-april-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 10th April Morning Shift","permalink":"pthe-sum-of-lone-pairs-present-on-the-central-atom-of-the-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-3uz97o0so86hjsqf","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>The sum of lone pairs present on the central atom of the interhalogen IF<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.101ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -320.9 436.6 486.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and IF<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.117ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -328 436.6 493.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is _________</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"1","explanation":"<p>Interhalogen compounds are the substances that consist of two different halogens. The most common type of interhalogen compounds are binary, containing only two different elements.</p>\n<p>In IF<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.101ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -320.9 436.6 486.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, iodine (I) is the central atom. Iodine has 7 valence electrons, 5 of which are used for bonding with the 5 fluorine (F) atoms. This leaves 2 electrons, or 1 lone pair on the iodine atom.</p>\n<p>In IF<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.117ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -328 436.6 493.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, iodine (I) is the central atom again. Iodine has 7 valence electrons, all of which are used for bonding with the 7 fluorine (F) atoms. So, there are no lone pairs on the iodine atom.</p>\n<p>Therefore, the sum of lone pairs present on the central atom of the interhalogens IF<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.101ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -320.9 436.6 486.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and IF<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.117ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -328 436.6 493.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is 1.</p>\n"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>अंतरा हैलोजन <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.282ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1450.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\"></use><use data-c=\"46\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-46\" transform=\"translate(361,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1047,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> एवं <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.282ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1450.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\"></use><use data-c=\"46\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-46\" transform=\"translate(361,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1047,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> के केन्द्रीय परमाणु पर उपस्थित एकाकी युग्मों की संख्या है:</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"1","explanation":null}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"hybridization-and-vsepr-theory","type":"integer","year":2023,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2023-online-10th-april-morning-shift","active":true},{"question_id":"1lgyhok29","chapter":"structure-of-atom","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2023-online-10th-april-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 10th April Morning Shift","permalink":"pthe-number-of-incorrect-statements-about-the-black-body-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-ccndl7i1lgqofifv","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>The number of incorrect statement/s about the black body from the following is __________</p>\n<p>(A) Emit or absorb energy in the form of electromagnetic radiation.</p>\n<p>(B) Frequency distribution of the emitted radiation depends on temperature.</p>\n<p>(C) At a given temperature, intensity vs frequency curve passes through a maximum value.</p>\n<p>(D) The maximum of the intensity vs frequency curve is at a higher frequency at higher temperature compared to that at lower temperature.</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"0","explanation":"<p>All the statements (A, B, C, D) provided about black bodies are correct. </p>\n<p>(A) A black body is an idealized physical body that absorbs all incident electromagnetic radiation, regardless of frequency or angle of incidence. It also emits energy in the form of electromagnetic radiation.</p>\n<p>(B) The frequency distribution of the emitted radiation by a black body indeed depends on its temperature. This phenomenon is described by Planck&#39;s law.</p>\n<p>(C) The intensity vs frequency curve for a black body, also known as the Planck&#39;s curve, does indeed pass through a maximum value for a given temperature.</p>\n<p>(D) The frequency at which the maximum intensity occurs increases with the temperature of the black body. This is stated in Wien&#39;s displacement law.</p>\n<p>So, the number of incorrect statements about the black body from the above is 0.</p>\n"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>किसी कृष्णिका (Black body) के संदर्भ में, निम्न में से असत्य कथनों की संख्या है:</p>\n<p>(A) विद्युत चुम्बकीय विकिरण के रूप में उर्जा को उत्सर्जित या अवशोषित करती है।</p>\n<p>(B) उत्सर्जित विकिरण का आवृत्ति वितरण तापमान पर निर्भर करता है।</p>\n<p>(C) किसी दिए गए तापमान पर, तीव्रता vs आवृत्ति वक्र एक उच्चिष्ठ मान से होकर गुजरता है।</p>\n<p>(D) तीव्रता vs आवृत्ति वक्र का उच्चिष्ठ, निम्न तापमान की तुलना में, उच्च तापमान पर उच्च आवृत्ति पर होता है।</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"0","explanation":null}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"photoelectric-effect","type":"integer","year":2023,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["multi_statements"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2023-online-10th-april-morning-shift","active":true},{"question_id":"1lgyhqmhf","chapter":"chemical-kinetics-and-nuclear-chemistry","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2023-online-10th-april-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 10th April Morning Shift","permalink":"pa-molecule-undergoes-two-independent-first-order-reaction-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-ppyuxkub6nqjzpqz","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>A molecule undergoes two independent first order reactions whose respective half lives are 12 min and 3 min. If both the reactions are occurring then the time taken for the 50% consumption of the reactant is ___________ min. (Nearest integer)</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"2","explanation":"<p>In the given problem, a molecule is undergoing two separate, simultaneous first-order reactions. Each of these reactions has its own rate constant and half-life. The half-life (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.622ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 717 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) of a first-order reaction is related to its rate constant (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.179ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 521 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D458\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D458\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) by the equation:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.798ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.013ex\" height=\"3.167ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1047.1 3984 1399.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(994.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(2050.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,516.8) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(278,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(834,0)\"><use data-c=\"2061\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2061\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(834,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1223,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1723,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(782.5,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D458\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D458\"></use></g><rect width=\"1693.4\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>When two or more first-order reactions are occurring independently and simultaneously (also known as parallel or competing reactions), the overall rate constant for the disappearance of the reactant is the sum of the rate constants for the individual reactions:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.72ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16.282ex\" height=\"2.29ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 7196.4 1012.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D458\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D458\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(554,-176.7) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">total</text></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3003.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(4058.9,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D458\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D458\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(554,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5238.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(6238.9,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D458\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D458\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(554,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Conversely, the overall half-life for the disappearance of the reactant is determined by the reciprocal of the sum of the reciprocals of the individual half-lives:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.29ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16.495ex\" height=\"3.246ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 7290.9 1434.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1029,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(617,-176.7) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">total</text></g></g></g><rect width=\"2171.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2689.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(3745.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(404,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(617,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"921.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5129.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(6129.3,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(404,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(617,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"921.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>This equation reflects the fact that the reactant is disappearing more quickly than it would due to any single reaction, because it is being consumed by two reactions at once.</p>\n<p>Substituting the given half-lives of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.507ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -666 1000 666\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> minutes and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.131ex\" height=\"1.554ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\